{"slug": "nth-term-of-a-sequence", "lang": "PYTHON 3", "code": "import sys\n\nMOD = 10**9 + 7\n\ndef main():\n    N = int(sys.stdin.readline().strip())\n    # The sequence is: 2, 6, 11, 17, 24, ...\n    # Differences: 4, 5, 6, 7, ...\n    # a(1) = 2\n    # a(n) = a(n-1) + (n+2) for n >= 2\n    # a(n) = 2 + sum(i=2 to n) (i+2) = 2 + sum(i=2 to n) i + 2*(n-1)\n    #      = 2 + (n(n+1)/2 - 1) + 2n - 2\n    #      = 1 + n(n+1)/2 + 2n - 2\n    #      = n(n+1)/2 + 2n - 1\n    #      = n(n+1)/2 + 2n - 1\n    #      = n(n+1)/2 + (4n - 2)/2\n    #      = (n(n+1) + 4n - 2)/2\n    #      = (n\u00b2 + n + 4n - 2)/2\n    #      = (n\u00b2 + 5n - 2)/2\n    # Let's verify: n=5: (25 + 25 - 2)/2 = 48/2 = 24 \u2713\n    # n=19: (361 + 95 - 2)/2 = 454/2 = 227 \u2713\n    result = (N * N + 5 * N - 2) // 2\n    result = result % MOD\n    print(result)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n", "local_ok": true, "err": ""}